# E-Commerce Platform (Next.js + Prisma)

Production-ready e-commerce template built with Next.js (pages router), React (TypeScript), PostgreSQL, and Prisma. Includes public storefront, cart/checkout, user accounts, and admin panel with product/order management.

## Project Structure
```
.
├── pages
│   ├── index.tsx                 # Home
│   ├── products/                 # Listing + product details
│   ├── category/[slug].tsx       # Category listing
│   ├── cart.tsx                  # Cart view
│   ├── checkout.tsx              # Checkout flow
│   ├── login.tsx / register.tsx  # Auth pages
│   ├── account/orders            # Customer order history
│   ├── admin                     # Admin dashboard + CRUD
│   └── api                       # Next.js API routes (auth, products, cart, orders, stats)
├── prisma
│   ├── schema.prisma             # Data model
│   └── seed.ts                   # Seed admin + sample data
├── lib
│   ├── prisma.ts                 # Prisma client singleton
│   ├── auth.ts                   # JWT helpers + guards
│   └── validators.ts             # Zod validation schemas
├── styles/globals.css            # Base styling
├── package.json
├── tsconfig.json
└── .env.example
```

## Environment Variables
Create `.env` (or export via your secret manager):
```
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@localhost:5432/ecommerce"
JWT_SECRET="supersecretjwt"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:3000"
```

## Prisma Schema (summary)
Key models: `User`, `Category`, `Product`, `Cart`, `CartItem`, `Address`, `Order`, `OrderItem` plus `Role` and `OrderStatus` enums. See [`prisma/schema.prisma`](prisma/schema.prisma) for the full definition.

## Next.js Routes (pages router)
- Storefront: `/`, `/products`, `/products/[slug]`, `/category/[slug]`
- User: `/login`, `/register`, `/cart`, `/checkout`, `/account/orders`, `/account/orders/[id]`
- Admin: `/admin`, `/admin/products`, `/admin/products/new`, `/admin/products/[id]`, `/admin/orders`, `/admin/orders/[id]`
- APIs: `/api/auth/login`, `/api/auth/register`, `/api/products`, `/api/products/[id]`, `/api/categories`, `/api/categories/[id]`, `/api/cart`, `/api/orders`, `/api/orders/[id]`, `/api/orders/checkout`, `/api/admin/stats`

## How to Run
1. Install dependencies:
   ```bash
   npm install
   ```
2. Generate Prisma client and run migrations:
   ```bash
   npx prisma generate
   npx prisma migrate dev --name init
   ```
3. Seed database (creates admin user `admin@example.com` / `admin123` plus sample catalog):
   ```bash
   npx prisma db seed --preview-feature || npm run prisma:seed
   ```
4. Start development server:
   ```bash
   npm run dev
   ```

## Notes
- Auth uses stateless JWT stored in HttpOnly cookie (`ecom_token`).
- Admin-only routes enforce `Role.ADMIN` guard in the API layer.
- Checkout creates orders from the authenticated user's cart and stores the shipping address record.
